# Collaborative Flexibility and Check-Ins

Use the approved plan as a guide, not a cage.

## Non-Negotiable Invariants (stay strict)

- Preserve security, auth ownership boundaries, and secret-safety requirements.
- Preserve data integrity and migration safety.
- Preserve agreed product outcomes and acceptance criteria unless the user approves a change.

## Flexible Execution (allowed without interruption)

- Adjust internal implementation details when user-visible behavior is unchanged.
- Refactor low-risk structure, naming, and test organization when it improves maintainability.
- Choose alternative technical paths if they better fit the codebase, while keeping outcomes intact.

## Mandatory Check-In Triggers

Pause and ask the user before proceeding when a discovered issue would change any of:

- Feature scope or priorities
- User-visible behavior or UX flow
- Data model semantics or retention policy
- Delivery timeline, complexity, or risk profile

## Communication Standard

- Briefly explain the issue, proposed options, and recommendation.
- Continue autonomously only after user confirmation when a trigger applies.
- If no trigger applies, proceed and report what changed and why.
